Probe timeouts and probe counts as quic-go computes them (hysteria client).

quic-go (vendor/quic-go/internal/utils/rtt_stats.go:68-77,
vendor/quic-go/internal/ackhandler/sent_packet_handler.go:30-31, :507-514, :677-683, :943-984):
  - before the first RTT sample the PTO is a flat 2 * DefaultInitialRTT = 200 ms, with no
    max_ack_delay;
  - the backoff is `PTO << ptoCount`, truncated at maxPTODuration = 60 s;
  - a timeout sends two probes, or one when nothing is in flight and the server's address is not
    validated yet, in the Initial space while those keys exist;
  - an acknowledgement clears ptoCount only once that address is validated.

Upstream ngtcp2 computes smoothed_rtt + 4*rttvar over the same initial RTT — 300 ms — shifts without
a ceiling (capping the count at 30 instead), sends ONE probe until its TLS handshake completes and
never two in the Initial space, and clears pto_count on any acknowledged ack-eliciting packet,
flooring it at 2.

This patch brings the four together for a client; the server paths keep upstream's shape.
Applies on top of 0003.

